<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dēmŏphŏon</span></b> ,
			ontis, m., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημοφόων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A son of Theseus and Phaedra, a lover of Phyllis,
				and one of those who fought before Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. R. Am. 597</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Verg. Cul. 130</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 2, 6,
				15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 24, 44</span></i> (3, 19, 28 M.); cf.
				<i><span class="en">Hyg.
				Fab. 59</span></i> and 243.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Aeneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				11, 675</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
